# ── Line endings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: ONE working tree is read by TWO gits. Windows git on E:\
# runs with core.autocrlf=true; WSL git on /mnt/e runs with it unset, which on
# Linux means false. Every tracked text file is stored LF and checked out CRLF, so
# Windows normalises CRLF→LF before comparing and reports a clean tree, while WSL
# compares raw bytes and reports the entire repo as modified. Neither is wrong —
# they are applying different rules to identical bytes. Attributes take precedence
# over core.autocrlf, so THIS file is what makes the two agree, and unlike a git
# config it travels with a clone instead of living on one machine.
#
# `eol=lf` is deliberate and stronger than a bare `text=auto`. `text=auto` alone
# fixes the COMPARISON but leaves the working tree native-per-platform — and
# "native" is precisely the concept with no single answer when two gits share one
# checkout. Pinning the tree to LF removes the ambiguity rather than papering over
# it: the bytes on disk stop flip-flopping, and a diff can never again show a whole
# file changed when only its line endings did.
#
# Blobs are unaffected. Every tracked text file is ALREADY stored LF — 136 of them,
# with 0 carrying CRLF in the index — so this rewrites nothing in history.

# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts MUST be LF: a CRLF shebang (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`) makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter named "bash\r" — a classic, confusing portability
# failure. Pinned explicitly because these are the files most likely to be run from
# the WSL side of this same tree.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# The source types this repo actually carries. Redundant under the glob above,
# stated so the policy reads without knowing how `text=auto` resolves each one.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.vue   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.mmd   text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these. `binary` disables line-ending conversion and
# text diffing both. Frontend/public/{favicon,brand-logo,images/og}/ and
# Frontend/design/brand/logo/png/ are documented to hold exactly these types.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
